+# Daily Grind rewards
+
+The existing homepage now includes a rewards registration form backed by a Node.js endpoint. Requires Node 24 or newer. Install with `pnpm install`; `pnpm start` serves the homepage and endpoint together. A static file host alone cannot perform registration.
+
+## Configuration
+
+- `PORT`: HTTP port (default `11222`).
+- `APP_ORIGIN`: exact public website origin, e.g. `https://coffee.example.com`. Required behind a production proxy; used for origin and token audience checks. Defaults to `http://localhost:11222` with the configured port.
+- `DATABASE_PATH`: persistent SQLite file, default `./data/rewards.sqlite`. Mount this directory on persistent storage. SQLite stores memberships and expiring single-use challenges; no raw tokens are stored. Use one service instance with this database.
+- `EVP_ORIGIN_TRIAL_TOKEN`: origin trial token for the public origin. When set, emitted as the `Origin-Trial` response header. Register for Chrome's Email Verification origin trial before enabling production use. Serve over HTTPS.
+
+## Verification flow
+
+The server renders a random challenge into `nonce` on the hidden `autocomplete="email-verification-token"` field, binding it to an HttpOnly session cookie. The browser fills the token during **native form submission**. Do not replace this with a submit-event `fetch` call: it may run before the browser fills the token.
+
+`POST /api/rewards/register` accepts URL-encoded `name`, `email`, `terms=yes`, and `evt`. The endpoint consumes the session challenge once, discovers the issuer through the email domain's DNS TXT record, fetches its well-known metadata and JWKS, checks the issuer signature and claims, then verifies the browser key binding, exact origin, nonce, timestamp, and SHA-256 hash. Provider requests use HTTPS, public address validation and pinned DNS, size/time limits, and no redirects. Symmetric and unsigned JWTs are rejected. Both current Ed25519 and legacy trial EdDSA names are accepted for compatibility.
+
+Only a successfully verified email creates a member. Missing tokens, unsupported providers or browsers, denied permissions, expired sessions, and invalid proofs show an actionable message without creating an account or sending email. A successful registration returns HTML with status 201; invalid verification returns 422, duplicate email 409, and invalid session/input 400. The flow creates a rewards membership, not a logged-in account session.
+
+## Checks
+
+`pnpm build` performs syntax validation without importing or running the server. `pnpm test` runs isolated crypto and database tests; it never imports the server entrypoint, starts a listener, or contacts an email provider. No browser verification was performed.
+
+## Protocol references
+
+- [Chrome Email Verification integration and origin trial](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/email-verification)
+- [Browser Email Verification API](https://wicg.github.io/email-verification/)
+- [Email Verification Protocol draft](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-hardt-email-verification-02)
